cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sparrow, please cite it as below."
title: "Sparrow: a temporal diagnostic log and data server"
abstract: >-
  Sparrow is a Rust service that turns scattered operational artifacts into
  retained evidence that agents can discover, inspect, correlate and query as a
  semantic graph. It ingests JSON/JSONL, Markdown, structured logs, syslog and
  unformatted text through typed Cap'n Proto RPC, durable directory consumption
  and active-log tailing. It stores exact source bytes in RocksDB with
  content-addressed deduplication and compression, retains them for a bounded
  window from acceptance under an explicit disk budget, and protects selected
  evidence with named, expiring pins. Persistent full-text and RDF 1.2 quad
  indexes, built on PurRDF, answer field, text and SPARQL 1.2 queries with
  explicit coverage and refusal reporting, through a CLI, a stdio MCP adapter
  and a Rust producer client with a composable tracing layer.
type: software
